%%%
export const meta = { title: "Nota Mega-Test" };

const Chip = (props: { children?: unknown }) => @span[class: "chip"]{@(props.children)};
const Aside = (props: { children?: unknown }) => @aside{@(props.children)};
const Colorized = (props: { children?: unknown }) => {
  let [color, setColor] = createSignal("red");
  return @span[onClick: () => setColor("green")][style: {color: color()}]{@(props.children)};
};

const name = "Will";
const url = "/home";
const disabled = true;
const rest = { id: "demo" };
const items = ["x", "y", "z"];
const i = 1;
const ui = { Card: Chip };
const comps = { card: Chip };
const k = "card";
const getTag = () => "em";
%%%

# Nota Mega-Test

A *terse* tour of _every_ Nota feature, written by @name,
spanning a soft line break.

@Aside{A block component nesting @b{markup} and an empty @span{}.}

## Elements & props

A @a[href:"/x"][title:"home"]{static link}, a @a[href:url]{dynamic link}, and an
@input[type:"text", disabled, ...rest] self-closing field; balanced braces stay literal:
@em{a set {1, 2, 3}}.

A markup-valued prop on a block element, at block position:

@figure[cap:@em{a caption}]{The figure body.}

Dynamic tags (all inline here): @(Chip){direct}, @(ui.Card){member}, @(getTag()){call},
@(comps[k])[n:1]{computed}. Also a @{bare @b{fragment}} and an expression @(1 + 2).

## Control flow

@if (items.length > 2) {Many}
else if (items.length > 0) {Some}
else {None} items.

@ul{
  @for (x of items) {@li{@x}}
  @for ([key, val] of [["a", 1], ["b", 2]]) {@li{@key = @val}}
  @for ({ id } of [{ id: 1 }, { id: 2 }]) {@if (id) {@li{row @id}}}
}

## Markup sugar

Emphasis nests: *bold with _italic_ within*; intra-word stays literal in my_var_name and 2*3*4.

###### A level-6 heading

- bullet one
- bullet two
  - nested bullet
- bullet three with a
  wrapped continuation line
+ ordered one
+ ordered two
1. explicit one
2. explicit two

## Raw spans

Inline `f(x)` code, math $x^2$ with a literal $a_@i$ and armed interpolation $b_|@i$ and
$c_|@(i + 1)$, and fence-form display math:

$$
\sum_|@(items.length) x_i
$$

Escapes render literally: \* \_ \# \$ \@ \{ \} and a backslash \\.

```python
def f(x):
    return x
```

@pre|{
@foo{x} is raw; |@Colorized{this is a child} and |@name interpolates.
}|

